+---
+id: dl-002-long-rental-discount-10-from-3-days-rounded-to-the-nearest-cent
+type: decision-log
+title: "Long-rental discount: 10% from 3 days, rounded to the nearest cent"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+<!-- decision-log body. `wingfoil memory add` copies this scaffold, setting only `id`, `title` and
+     `status` (and any `--tags` or `--set` value). Fill the required frontmatter fields and replace
+     these placeholder comments yourself; `wingfoil memory submit` then checks the required fields,
+     moves `status` forward and commits the document as you left it, naming in the commit body the
+     content it carries. -->
+
+## Context
+
+The school wants to reward longer stays: a rental of 3 days or more costs 10% less than its full price.
+Money is in whole euro cents (dl-001), and 90% of a total is not always a whole number of cents.
+
+## Decision
+
+- The threshold is 3 days, inclusive, counted in whole days of the rental period.
+- The discount applies to the whole rental total, not only to the days beyond the third.
+- The reduced total is `round(total x 90 / 100)`, to the nearest cent, halves rounded up. Integer
+  arithmetic keeps the result deterministic.
+- The threshold and rate are named constants in `src/index.ts`; `quote` and `book` share the pricing.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Totals stay integer cents. A 3-day rental can cost less than a 2-day one, which follows from the rule
+as stated. A change of rate or threshold is a change to the two constants.
